hibition":"Edvard Munch","date_start":"1927-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","date_end":"1927-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"Nationalgalerie, Berlin"},{"exhibition":"Edvard Munch, angst/anxiety","date_start":"2012-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","date_end":"2013-02-17T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"ARoS Aarhus Kunstmuseum"},{"exhibition":"Becoming Edvard Munch: Influence, Anxiety, and Myth","date_start":"2009-02-15T00:00:00.000Z","date_end":"2009-04-26T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"The Art Institute of Chicago"},{"exhibition":"Edvard Munch Portraits","date_start":"2025-03-20T00:00:00.000Z","date_end":"2025-06-29T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"National Portrait Gallery"},{"exhibition":"Edvard Munchs Maleriutstilling","date_start":"1892-09-14T00:00:00.000Z","date_end":"1892-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"Juveler Tostrups Gaard Kristiania"},{"exhibition":"Eduard Munch. Gemälde-Ausstellung","date_start":"1893-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","venue":"Unter den Linden, Berlin"}],"inscriptions":[{"content":"E. Munch","type":"signature"}],"labels":[{"text":"The image is divided vertically into two almost equal\r\nhalves. To the left, a man and woman stand in the shade on\r\na veranda, while to the right a view of a lush, sun-drenched\r\ncoastal landscape opens up before us. A perfect setting\r\nfor a romantic tale from the bright Nordic summer nights.\r\nInstead, however, we witness a chilling chamber play about\r\nemotional coldness and distance.\r\nThroughout his life, Edvard Munch was preoccupied\r\nwith psychologically stunted romantic relationships. The\r\ninterest first manifested in this big picture. As models, he\r\nused the Norwegian theatre critic Sigurd Bødtker and his own\r\nyoungest sister, Inger, but the accuracy of their likenesses\r\nis not important here. Rather, they have been cast in roles:\r\nInger, who was 21 years old at the time, is portrayed as a\r\nmiddle-aged woman. Her closed-off body language forms\r\na distancing counterpoint to the posing man.\r\nThe picture was painted in the summer of 1889, when\r\nMunch settled at Åsgårdstrand, a fishing village on the west\r\nside of the Oslo fjord. Its coastal landscape would go on to\r\nappear as the poignantly animated panorama seen in the\r\nbackground of several of Munch’s best-known images (50 Favorites in the SMK Collection).","type":"CATALOGUETEXT","source":"Peter Nørgaard Larsen","date":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"text":"In the summer of 1889 Munch settled by Åsgårdstrand on the west side of the Oslo fiord. Here, he staged his tales of absence and loneliness with theatre critic Sigurd Bødtker and his youngest sister Inger as models. Accurate resemblance is, however, unimportant. She appears as a middle-aged, disillusioned woman whose closed-up body language provides an icy foil to the posing aesthete. The painting is an example of Munch’s break with realism. Paints are applied in rapid, transparent brushstrokes that disengage colour from objects, imbuing it with painterly value in its own right. He also makes the bold move of working with a vertical division of the picture plane, employing the contrast between the sunlit landscape and the dark porch to poignant effect.","type":"EXHIBITIONTEXT","source":"Peter Nørgaard Larsen"}],"materials":["canvas"],"object_names":[{"name":"Painting"}],"production":[{"creator":"Munch, Edvard","creator_forename":"Edvard","creator_surname":"Munch","creator_date_of_birth":"1863-12-12T00:00:00.000Z","creator_date_of_death":"1944-01-23T00:00:00.000Z","creator_nationality":"Norwegian","creator_gender":"MALE","creator_lref":"1810_person"}],"production_date":[{"start":"1889-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","end":"1889-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","period":"1889"}],"techniques":["Oil on canvas"],"titles":[{"title":"Summer Evening","language":"engelsk"},{"title":"Summer Evening","notes":"Titel tidligere anvendt på SMK","type":"previous title","language":"engelsk"}],"number_of_parts":1,"object_number":"KMS2070","object_url":"https://api.smk.dk/api/v1/art?object_number=KMS2070","frontend_url":"https://open.smk.dk/artwork/image/KMS2070","iiif_manifest":"https://api.smk.dk/api/v1/iiif/manifest?id=KMS2070","enrichment_url":"https://enrichment.api.smk.dk/api/enrichment/KMS2070","similar_images_url":"https://similar.api.smk.dk/similar/?object_number=KMS2070","production_dates_notes":["Værkdatering: (1889)","Maleriet er udateret, men der er almindelig enighed om, at det er udført i sommeren 1889 (jf. Woll, 2008)."],"public_domain":true,"rights":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/","on_display":true,"alternative_images":[{"mime_type":"image/tiff","iiif_id":"https://iip.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/0z708x22n_KMS2070.tif.jp2","iiif_info":"https://iip.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/0z708x22n_KMS2070.tif.jp2/info.json","width":14994,"height":11607,"size":180046903.44827586,"thumbnail":"https://iip-thumb.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/0z708x22n_KMS2070.tif.jp2/full/!1024,/0/default.jpg","native":"https://iip.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/0z708x22n_KMS2070.tif.jp2/full/full/0/native.jpg","orientation":"landscape"}],"image_mime_type":"image/tiff","image_iiif_id":"https://iip.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/x346d7279_KMS2070.tif.reconstructed.tif.jp2","image_iiif_info":"https://iip.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/x346d7279_KMS2070.tif.reconstructed.tif.jp2/info.json","image_width":4939,"image_height":3867,"image_size":16248666,"image_thumbnail":"https://iip-thumb.smk.dk/iiif/jp2/x346d7279_KMS2070.tif.reconstructed.tif.jp2/full/!1024,/0/default.jpg","image_native":"https://api.smk.dk/api/v1/download/W3siaW1nX3VybCI6Imh0dHBzOi8vaWlwLnNtay5kay9paWlmL2pwMi94MzQ2ZDcyNzlfS01TMjA3MC50aWYucmVjb25zdHJ1Y3RlZC50aWYuanAyL2Z1bGwvZnVsbC8wL25hdGl2ZS5qcGciLCJwdWJsaWNfZG9tYWluIjp0cnVlLCJvYmplY3RfbnVtYmVyIjoiS01TMjA3MCIsIm51bSI6IiJ9XQ==/KMS2070.jpg","image_cropped":true,"image_orientation":"landscape","image_hq":true,"has_3d_file":false,"has_image":true,"colors":["#222222","#77733d","#335c2d","#dddddd","#795025","#73a1d2","#908d41"],"suggested_bg_color":["#908d41"],"entropy":9.777474,"contrast":3.0982563,"saturation":2.6645215,"colortemp":3.4696112,"brightness":4.135266,"ha